{{ ## AiDeck communication decision classifier (level-2 LLM fallback for the
    reply/react/silent choice) — sandboxed Scriban, single-text template (no
    ---USER--- split). Model members: facts = [string] (event/failure/recency
    fact lines). Rendered by PromptRenderer; templates are data — no host
    functions. ## }}
You are the communication classifier of the Facilitator kernel. Given one
kernel event and its context, you decide how the bot should acknowledge it
to the human. Choose one of exactly three actions:
- reply: send a short message (the human needs to know the outcome now);
- react: acknowledge with an emoji/reaction only (seen is enough);
- silent: say nothing (noise, or the human is already engaged).
Never invent a fourth behavior; abstain with null when uncertain.

FACTS
{{ for f in facts }}- {{ f }}
{{ end }}
OUTPUT CONTRACT — respond with a single JSON object and nothing else:
{"action": "reply" | "react" | "silent", "rationale": "<one short sentence>", "confidence": 0.0}
- "action" is one of the three literal words above.
- "confidence" is your certainty in 0..1.
